---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { release } from '../data/release';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<Base title="Get the Android app" description="Download fairenough for Android, check the signing identity, and keep your records when updating.">
  <div class="wrap inner-page"><header class="page-head"><h1>{release.published ? 'Your next journey starts here.' : 'The first release, in preparation.'}</h1><p class="lead">An Android installation file, called an APK. Android {release.minimumAndroid} or later. Your records stay on your device.</p></header>
    <section class="download-panel" aria-labelledby="release-title"><div><h2 id="release-title">fairenough {release.version}</h2><p>{release.published ? `Released ${release.date}` : 'The first public release is being prepared.'}</p><p>Undergraduate train passes. MRT and LRT. Saved route fares.</p></div>{release.published ? <a class="button" href={release.apk}>Download APK <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a> : <a class="button" href={release.url}>View releases <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>}</section>
    <article class="prose"><h2>Install once. Keep your records.</h2><ol><li>Download the APK from the GitHub release.</li><li>Open it on your Android phone. If Android asks, allow installation from the browser or file manager you are using.</li><li>Install fairenough and set up the actual dates and price of your pass.</li></ol><p>For updates, install the new signed APK over the existing app. Do not uninstall first. Create a backup before updating.</p><p>The release includes a SHA-256 file checksum. The repository also documents the app's signing certificate. A matching checksum checks the downloaded file; the certificate identifies its signer.</p><h2>What the first version calculates</h2><p>It compares recorded regular adult fares with the undergraduate train pass price. You save an LTA-checked fare for each route and fare period. Individual corrections account for known discounts. Missing fares are clearly marked.</p><p><a href={`${base}docs/getting-started/`}>Get started</a> or <a href={`${base}docs/backups-and-updates/`}>read the backup and update guide</a>.</p></article>
  </div>
</Base>
